  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Alliance Africa - Knowledge Transfer Network Ltd</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Knowledge Transfer Network&apos;s (KTN) Global Alliance Africa programme aims to create more effective and output-driven technology and innovation ecosystems in Nigeria, South Africa, Kenya and adjacent countries to underpin a more self-sustaining economy to help meet the long-term socio-economic needs in Africa. It aims to do this by establishing a knowledge transfer network between the UK and the three African countries (and wider regionally) to fuel greater innovation partnership in alignment with HMG Aid Strategy. It also aims to support a more cohesive and strategic approach for HMG Aid initiatives underpinned by innovation in Africa to for greater synergies and impacts.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UKAfrica KTN is a six year project designed to strengthen and scale local innovation and business environments in Kenya, Nigeria and South Africa. The project coordinates networking activities that can help foster longlasting, strategic partnerships between the three countries, their neighbours and the UK. COVID-19</narrative>
  </description>
